build: 2026-06-23 v10.65.0 (Audio-Input Live Monitoring + FeedbackGuard)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: Founder request — "Audio Input Live Monitoring mit Feedback unterdrücken". Tools ▸ Audio In now has a "Live monitoring" toggle: routes the mic through the main output (sing/play over the beat) with a monitor-level control (EchoelValueField) and a live FeedbackGuard. FeedbackGuard (the pure, unit-tested core, finally wired) watches the output RMS and the instant a rising-over-ceiling runaway starts — the acoustic-feedback signature — it ducks the MIC monitor (not the music) and shows a "ducking" indicator; releases when safe. Implemented WITHOUT an audio-thread tap or @Sendable self-capture: the duck runs on the existing MainActor meter poll (~15 Hz), so there's zero render-thread risk. Default OFF and fully guarded (no mic permission / no input format → toggle reverts, never crashes); a headphones/interface hint explains the only way to remove the acoustic loop entirely. AudioEngine.setInputMonitoring connects inputNode → monitorMixer → masterMixer with the proven pause/connect/restart pattern. Notch (FeedbackGuard.ringingBin) + Apple voice-processing AEC are the device-verified v2 (kept out of v1 to avoid reconfiguring the shared playback engine blind). iOS-only; compile gate validates. Device-verify the monitoring/feedback behaviour on hardware.
